enburg-Strelitz district (the former Lordship of Stargard), and the western Principality of Ratzeburg exclave (the former Prince-Bishopric of Ratzeburg), which lay mostly in the west of the modern Nordwestmecklenburg district. At the time of its establishment, the main part of the duchy bordered on the territory of Swedish Pomerania in the north and of Brandenburg in the south; Ratzeburg bordered Saxe-Lauenburg and the Free City of Lübeck."},{"qid":"Q161215","from_t":1815,"to_t":1878,"method":"name-template+date","confidence":0.879818228850465,"label":"Grand Duchy of Mecklenburg-Strelitz","description":"grand duchy (1701–1918)","inception":1815.4876712328767,"dissolved":1918.145205479452,"enwiki":"Grand Duchy of Mecklenburg-Strelitz","summary":"The Grand Duchy of Mecklenburg-Strelitz was a territory in Northern Germany, held by the younger line of the House of Mecklenburg residing in Neustrelitz. Like the neighbouring Grand Duchy of Mecklenburg-Schwerin, it was a sovereign member state of the German Confederation and became a federated state of the North German Confederation and finally of the German Empire upon the unification in 1871. After World War I and the German Revolution of 1918–19 it was succeeded by the Free State of Mecklenburg-Strelitz."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q2751106","kind":"predecessor","value_qid":"Q109252949","value_label":"Duchy of Mecklenburg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P155","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Duchy of Mecklenburg"},{"qid":"Q2751106","kind":"successor","value_qid":"Q161215","value_label":"Grand Duchy of Mecklenburg-Strelitz","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1366","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Grand Duchy of Mecklenburg-Strelitz"},{"qid":"Q2751106","kind":"flag","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Flagge Großherzogtümer Mecklenburg.svg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P41","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null},{"qid":"Q2751106","kind":"coat","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Wappen M